New building materials refer to novel materials applied in the construction field, characterized by their ability to meet diverse requirements such as high performance, high reliability, environmental friendliness, and aesthetic appeal, while changing and innovating traditional construction methods and structural forms. This article provides a literature review covering the types, applications, and development trends of new building materials.

I. Types of New Building Materials
1. Carbon fiber concrete: Composed of carbon fiber, cement, and aggregates, with high tensile strength and toughness;
2. Color-coated steel plates: Made of color-coated steel sheets and thermal insulation materials, suitable for industrial plants and civil building exterior decoration;
3. Smart glass: Capable of changing light transmission and controlling indoor temperature and shading;
4. Ultra-high performance concrete: Possessing extremely high seismic resistance and compressive strength;
5. Polyurethane insulation boards: Effective for heat insulation and fire prevention, suitable for building exterior wall insulation and waterproofing;
6. Clay bricks: Having good thermal protection and acoustic properties;
7. Eco-friendly wood: Made from natural plant fibers, with good environmental performance and aesthetics.

II. Application Areas of New Building Materials
New building materials have wide applications, mainly including:
1. Building exterior decoration: Such as color-coated steel plates and curtain walls;
2. Building sound and heat insulation: Such as polyurethane insulation boards and graphene;
3. Building structure: Such as carbon fiber reinforcement and ultra-high performance concrete;
4. Building foundation and environment: Such as eco-friendly wood and green materials;
5. Building equipment: Such as smart home systems and photovoltaic materials.

III. Development Trends of New Building Materials
1. Environmental performance: Environmental protection will become an important direction;
2. Smart features: With technological advancement, focus will increase on smart features and supporting equipment;
3. Lightweight: With urbanization and population growth, emphasis will be on lightweight materials;
4. Functionality: New building materials will expand their applications to meet diverse construction needs.

